cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZenoFCIS, please cite this software."
title: ZenoFCIS
authors:
  - given-names: Dana
    family-names: Edwards
    alias: TheDarkLightX
version: 2.6.0
# date-released: Set the release date during the release step.
license: [MIT, Apache-2.0]
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheDarkLightX/ZenoFCIS"
abstract: >-
  ZenoFCIS is a software factory that combines human intent, large language
  model proposals, and symbolic checking to develop bounded software contracts
  and implementations. Humans define requirements and review results; language
  models propose candidate programs and explanations; deterministic checkers
  assess declared properties within explicit supported domains. The factory
  separates pure decisions from effects and retains evidence for review.
keywords:
  - software factory
  - human and LLM collaboration
  - symbolic verification
  - program synthesis
  - functional core
